{"strongs": "H3320", "word": "יָצַב", "translit": "ya.tsav", "root": "יצב", "morph": "H:V", "pos": "verb", "gloss": "set or station oneself, take one's stand", "definition": "[ יָצַב ] verb only Hithpa`el set or station oneself, take one's stand ( ᵑ7 יצב Pa`el & derivatives; Arabic be constant, firm ) — Hithpa`el Perfect 3 plural הִתְיַצְּבוּ 2Chr 11:13 ׳ וְהִת consecutive Num 11:16 Imperfect יִתְיַצֵּב Deut 7:24 + 6 t.; יִתְיַצָּ֑ב Job 41:2 יִתְיַצַּ֑ב Prov 22:29 וַיִּתְיַצֵּב 1Sam 3:10 + 5 t.; 3 feminine singular וַתֵּתַצֵּב Exod 2:4 (but read וַתִּתְיַצֵּב compare Sam Ges «GKC:71»§ 71 Kö i, 430 ); 2 masculine singular תִּתְיַצֵּב 2Sam 18:13 וְאֶתְיַצְּבָה Hab 2:1 יִתְיַצְּבוּ Ps 2:2 + 2 t.; וַיִּתְיַצְּבוּ Exod 19:17 + 4 t.; Imperative הִתְיַצֵּב Exod 8:16 + 5 t.: הִתְיַצְּבוּ 1Sam 10:19 + 6 t.; infinitive construct (מֵ)הִתְיַצֵּב 2Sam 21:5 + 4 t.; — station oneself, take one's stand, stand: \\ \\ a. with phrase of place, Exod 2:4 ( E , with מֵרָחוֺק ), 2Sam 18:13 (with מִנֶּגֶד ), figurative = stand aloof ( VB Dr ); v 2Sam 18:30 (with כֹּה , || עָמַד ): with ב loc, Exod 19:17 ; Num 22:22 (both E ), Judg 20:2 ; Deut 31:14 (twice in verse), also (in sense of having a place or position ) נִשְׁמַדְנוּ מֵהִתְיַצֵּב בְּכָלגְּֿבֻל יִשְׂרָאֵל 2Sam 21:5 with בְּתוֺךְ person 1Sam 10:23 , location 2Sam 23:12 = 2Chr 11:14 with עַל location, at, by Num 23:3 ; Num 23:15 ( J E ), upon Hab 2:1 (|| עמד ), Ps 36:5 (figurative); with עַל person see below; with שָׁם and עִם person Exod 34:5 (subject ׳ י ), Num 11:16 (both J E ). \\ \\ b. absolute 1Sam 3:10 ( ׳ י subject); especially of standing quiet and passive, to see the mighty deliverance of ׳ י Exod 14:13 ( J ), 1Sam 12:7 ; 1Sam 12:16 ; 2Chr 20:17 (|| עמד ); of taking a stand to fight 1Sam 17:16 ; Ps 2:2 in military array Jer 46:4 (with ב accompare), v Jer 46:14 (|| הָכֵן לָךְ ); to answer a charge Job 33:5 וְיִתְיַצְּבוּ כְמוֺ לְבוּשׁ Job 38:14 and they (terrestrial things) stand forth (in the light) like a garment . \\ \\ c. with לִפְנֵי person = present oneself before Exod 8:16 ; Exod 9:13 (both J ), Prov 22:29 (twice in verse); ׳ לִפְנֵי י Josh 24:1 ( E ), 1Sam 10:19 (see also d ); so as servants or courtiers (see לְ 6 c ), with implication of readiness for service עַלאֲֿדֹנָי Zech 6:5 ׳ לְ י Job 1:6 ; Job 2:1 (twice in verse). \\ \\ d. with לְַ person take one's stand on the side of 2Chr 11:13 with ל , מִייִֿתְצֵּב לִי עִם Ps 94:16 who will take a stand forme against the workers of iniquity (|| מִי יָקוּם לִי עִם ); of holding one's ground , maintaining one's position before ׳ י ( לְנֶגֶד עֵינֶיךָ ׅ Ps 5:6 so with לִפְנֵי Josh 1:5 ( D ), Deut 9:2 ; Job 41:2 with בְּפָנֶיךָ Deut 7:24 ; Deut 11:25 absolute וְאֵין עִמְּךָ לְהִתִיַצֵּב 2Chr 20:6", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3665')\">BDB3665</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H3320')\">H3320</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3664')\">BDB3664</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3666')\">BDB3666</entry></div><p> [<bdbheb>יָצַב</bdbheb>] <b>verb</b> only <b>Hithpa`el</b> <highlightword>set or station oneself, take one's stand</highlightword> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Tg')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵑ7</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> <bdbheb>יצב</bdbheb> Pa`el &amp; derivatives; Arabic <placeholder2274/> <highlight>be constant, firm</highlight>) — <div class=\"point\"><b>Hithpa`el</b> <highlight>Perfect</highlight> 3 plural <bdbheb>הִתְיַצְּבוּ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"2Chr 11:13\" b=\"14\" cBegin=\"11\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"11\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(14,11,13)\">2Chr 11:13</ref> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>וְהִת</bdbheb> consecutive <ref ref=\"Num 11:16\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"11\" vBegin=\"16\" cEnd=\"11\" vEnd=\"16\" onclick=\"bcv(4,11,16)\">Num 11:16</ref> <highlight>Imperfect</highlight> <bdbheb>יִתְיַצֵּב</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Deut 7:24\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"24\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"24\" onclick=\"bcv(5,7,24)\">Deut 7:24</ref> + 6 t.; <bdbheb>יִתְיַצָּ֑ב</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Job 41:2\" b=\"18\" cBegin=\"41\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"41\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(18,41,2)\">Job 41:2</ref> <bdbheb>יִתְיַצַּ֑ב</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Prov 22:29\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"22\" vBegin=\"29\" cEnd=\"22\" vEnd=\"29\" onclick=\"bcv(20,22,29)\">Prov 22:29</ref> <bdbheb>וַיִּתְיַצֵּב</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"1Sam 3:10\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(9,3,10)\">1Sam 3:10</ref> + 5 t.; 3 feminine singular <bdbheb>וַתֵּתַצֵּב</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Exod 2:4\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(2,2,4)\">Exod 2:4</ref> (but read <bdbheb>וַתִּתְיַצֵּב</bdbheb> compare Sam <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Ges')\">Ges</lookup><sup>«GKC:71»§ 71</sup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Kö')\">Kö<sup>i, 430</sup></lookup>); 2 masculine singular <bdbheb>תִּתְיַצֵּב</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"2Sam 18:13\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"18\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"18\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(10,18,13)\">2Sam 18:13</ref> <bdbheb>וְאֶתְיַצְּבָה</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Hab 2:1\" b=\"35\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(35,2,1)\">Hab 2:1</ref> <bdbheb>יִתְיַצְּבוּ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ps 2:2\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(19,2,2)\">Ps 2:2</ref> + 2 t.; <bdbheb>וַיִּתְיַצְּבוּ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Exod 19:17\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"19\" vBegin=\"17\" cEnd=\"19\" vEnd=\"17\" onclick=\"bcv(2,19,17)\">Exod 19:17</ref> + 4 t.; <highlight>Imperative</highlight> <bdbheb>הִתְיַצֵּב</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Exod 8:16\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"8\" vBegin=\"16\" cEnd=\"8\" vEnd=\"16\" onclick=\"bcv(2,8,16)\">Exod 8:16</ref> + 5 t.: <bdbheb>הִתְיַצְּבוּ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"1Sam 10:19\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"19\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"19\" onclick=\"bcv(9,10,19)\">1Sam 10:19</ref> + 6 t.; <highlight>infinitive construct</highlight> <bdbheb>(מֵ)הִתְיַצֵּב</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"2Sam 21:5\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"21\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"21\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(10,21,5)\">2Sam 21:5</ref> + 4 t.; — <highlight>station oneself, take one's stand, stand:</highlight> <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>a.</b> with phrase of place, <ref ref=\"Exod 2:4\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(2,2,4)\">Exod 2:4</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('E')\"><reflink>E</reflink></lookup>, with <bdbheb>מֵרָחוֺק</bdbheb>), <ref ref=\"2Sam 18:13\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"18\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"18\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(10,18,13)\">2Sam 18:13</ref> (with <bdbheb>מִנֶּגֶד</bdbheb>), figurative = <highlight>stand aloof</highlight> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('VB')\"><reflink>VB</reflink></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Dr')\">Dr</lookup>); v<ref ref=\"2Sam 18:30\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"18\" vBegin=\"30\" cEnd=\"18\" vEnd=\"30\" onclick=\"bcv(10,18,30)\">2Sam 18:30</ref> (with <bdbheb>כֹּה</bdbheb>, || <bdbheb>עָמַד</bdbheb>): with <bdbheb>ב</bdbheb> loc, <ref ref=\"Exod 19:17\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"19\" vBegin=\"17\" cEnd=\"19\" vEnd=\"17\" onclick=\"bcv(2,19,17)\">Exod 19:17</ref>; <ref ref=\"Num 22:22\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"22\" vBegin=\"22\" cEnd=\"22\" vEnd=\"22\" onclick=\"bcv(4,22,22)\">Num 22:22</ref> (both <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('E')\"><reflink>E</reflink></lookup>), <ref ref=\"Judg 20:2\" b=\"7\" cBegin=\"20\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"20\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(7,20,2)\">Judg 20:2</ref>; <ref ref=\"Deut 31:14\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"31\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"31\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(5,31,14)\">Deut 31:14</ref> (twice in verse), also (in sense of <highlight>having a place</highlight> or <highlight>position</highlight>) <bdbheb>נִשְׁמַדְנוּ מֵהִתְיַצֵּב בְּכָלגְּֿבֻל יִשְׂרָאֵל</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"2Sam 21:5\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"21\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"21\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(10,21,5)\">2Sam 21:5</ref> with <bdbheb>בְּתוֺךְ</bdbheb> person <ref ref=\"1Sam 10:23\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"23\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"23\" onclick=\"bcv(9,10,23)\">1Sam 10:23</ref>, location <ref ref=\"2Sam 23:12\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"23\" vBegin=\"12\" cEnd=\"23\" vEnd=\"12\" onclick=\"bcv(10,23,12)\">2Sam 23:12</ref> = <ref ref=\"2Chr 11:14\" b=\"14\" cBegin=\"11\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"11\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(14,11,14)\">2Chr 11:14</ref> with <bdbheb>עַל</bdbheb> location, <highlight>at, by</highlight> <ref ref=\"Num 23:3\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"23\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"23\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(4,23,3)\">Num 23:3</ref>; <ref ref=\"Num 23:15\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"23\" vBegin=\"15\" cEnd=\"23\" vEnd=\"15\" onclick=\"bcv(4,23,15)\">Num 23:15</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('J')\"><reflink>J</reflink></lookup><lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('E')\"><reflink>E</reflink></lookup>), <highlight>upon</highlight> <ref ref=\"Hab 2:1\" b=\"35\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(35,2,1)\">Hab 2:1</ref> (|| <bdbheb>עמד</bdbheb>), <ref ref=\"Ps 36:5\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"36\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"36\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(19,36,5)\">Ps 36:5</ref> (figurative); with <bdbheb>עַל</bdbheb> person see below; with <bdbheb>שָׁם</bdbheb> and <bdbheb>עִם</bdbheb> person <ref ref=\"Exod 34:5\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"34\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"34\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(2,34,5)\">Exod 34:5</ref> (subject <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>י</bdbheb>), <ref ref=\"Num 11:16\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"11\" vBegin=\"16\" cEnd=\"11\" vEnd=\"16\" onclick=\"bcv(4,11,16)\">Num 11:16</ref> (both <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('J')\"><reflink>J</reflink></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('E')\"><reflink>E</reflink></lookup>). <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>b.</b> absolute <ref ref=\"1Sam 3:10\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(9,3,10)\">1Sam 3:10</ref> (<bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>י</bdbheb> subject); especially of standing quiet and passive, to see the mighty deliverance of <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>י</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Exod 14:13\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"14\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"14\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(2,14,13)\">Exod 14:13</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('J')\"><reflink>J</reflink></lookup>), <ref ref=\"1Sam 12:7\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(9,12,7)\">1Sam 12:7</ref>; <ref ref=\"1Sam 12:16\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"16\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"16\" onclick=\"bcv(9,12,16)\">1Sam 12:16</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Chr 20:17\" b=\"14\" cBegin=\"20\" vBegin=\"17\" cEnd=\"20\" vEnd=\"17\" onclick=\"bcv(14,20,17)\">2Chr 20:17</ref> (|| <bdbheb>עמד</bdbheb>); of taking a stand to fight <ref ref=\"1Sam 17:16\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"17\" vBegin=\"16\" cEnd=\"17\" vEnd=\"16\" onclick=\"bcv(9,17,16)\">1Sam 17:16</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ps 2:2\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(19,2,2)\">Ps 2:2</ref> in military array <ref ref=\"Jer 46:4\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"46\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"46\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(24,46,4)\">Jer 46:4</ref> (with <bdbheb>ב</bdbheb> accompare), v<ref ref=\"Jer 46:14\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"46\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"46\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(24,46,14)\">Jer 46:14</ref> (|| <bdbheb>הָכֵן לָךְ</bdbheb>); to answer a charge <ref ref=\"Job 33:5\" b=\"18\" cBegin=\"33\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"33\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(18,33,5)\">Job 33:5</ref> <bdbheb>וְיִתְיַצְּבוּ כְמוֺ לְבוּשׁ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Job 38:14\" b=\"18\" cBegin=\"38\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"38\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(18,38,14)\">Job 38:14</ref> <highlight>and they</highlight> (terrestrial things) <highlight>stand forth</highlight> (in the light) <highlight>like a garment</highlight>. <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>c.</b> with <bdbheb>לִפְנֵי</bdbheb> person = <highlight>present oneself before</highlight> <ref ref=\"Exod 8:16\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"8\" vBegin=\"16\" cEnd=\"8\" vEnd=\"16\" onclick=\"bcv(2,8,16)\">Exod 8:16</ref>; <ref ref=\"Exod 9:13\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"9\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"9\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(2,9,13)\">Exod 9:13</ref> (both <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('J')\"><reflink>J</reflink></lookup>), <ref ref=\"Prov 22:29\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"22\" vBegin=\"29\" cEnd=\"22\" vEnd=\"29\" onclick=\"bcv(20,22,29)\">Prov 22:29</ref> (twice in verse); <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>לִפְנֵי י</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Josh 24:1\" b=\"6\" cBegin=\"24\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"24\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(6,24,1)\">Josh 24:1</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('E')\"><reflink>E</reflink></lookup>), <ref ref=\"1Sam 10:19\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"19\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"19\" onclick=\"bcv(9,10,19)\">1Sam 10:19</ref> (see also <b>d</b>); so as servants or courtiers (see  <bdbheb><reflink>לְ</reflink></bdbheb> <b>6 c</b>), with implication of readiness for service <bdbheb>עַלאֲֿדֹנָי</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Zech 6:5\" b=\"38\" cBegin=\"6\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"6\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(38,6,5)\">Zech 6:5</ref> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>לְ י</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Job 1:6\" b=\"18\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(18,1,6)\">Job 1:6</ref>; <ref ref=\"Job 2:1\" b=\"18\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(18,2,1)\">Job 2:1</ref> (twice in verse). <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>d.</b> with <bdbheb>לְַ</bdbheb> person <highlight>take one's stand on the side of</highlight> <ref ref=\"2Chr 11:13\" b=\"14\" cBegin=\"11\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"11\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(14,11,13)\">2Chr 11:13</ref> with <bdbheb>ל</bdbheb>, <bdbheb>מִייִֿתְצֵּב לִי עִם</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ps 94:16\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"94\" vBegin=\"16\" cEnd=\"94\" vEnd=\"16\" onclick=\"bcv(19,94,16)\">Ps 94:16</ref> <highlight>who will take a stand forme against</highlight> the workers of iniquity (|| <bdbheb>מִי יָקוּם לִי עִם</bdbheb>); of <highlight>holding one's ground</highlight>, maintaining one's position before <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>י</bdbheb> <bdbheb>( לְנֶגֶד עֵינֶיךָ ׅ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ps 5:6\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(19,5,6)\">Ps 5:6</ref> so with <bdbheb>לִפְנֵי</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Josh 1:5\" b=\"6\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(6,1,5)\">Josh 1:5</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('D')\"><reflink>D</reflink></lookup>), <ref ref=\"Deut 9:2\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"9\" vB